# CODEOWNERS for specora-verify
#
# This file maps directories to the maintainers responsible for reviewing
# changes in that area. It is read by GitHub to automatically request
# review from the right maintainer.
#
# Entries are kept in sync with MAINTAINERS.md. If the maintainer roster
# changes, update both files in the same pull request.
#
# The last matching pattern wins, so more-specific rules go last.
#
# Handle legend (see MAINTAINERS.md for affiliation and contact info):
#   @cho-cvc             — core verifier, wire-spec, CI, release engineering, crypto
#   @nickcontinentalvc   — provider audit-log readers, integration tests, reader docs

# Default owner — catches anything not otherwise assigned.
*                                       @cho-cvc

# Core library and CLI
/specora_verify/                        @cho-cvc
/specora_verify/canonical.py            @cho-cvc
/specora_verify/signature.py            @cho-cvc
/specora_verify/hash.py                 @cho-cvc
/specora_verify/cli.py                  @cho-cvc
/specora_verify/__init__.py             @cho-cvc

# Reader framework — Nick owns the readers themselves, Cho co-reviews any
# change that touches how readers map to the wire spec.
/specora_verify/readers/                @nickcontinentalvc @cho-cvc

# Tests mirror the layout of the code they exercise.
/tests/                                 @cho-cvc
/tests/readers/                         @nickcontinentalvc @cho-cvc
/tests/fixtures/                        @nickcontinentalvc @cho-cvc
/tests/test_wire_spec_schemas.py        @cho-cvc

# Documentation tree
/docs/                                  @cho-cvc
/docs/README.md                         @cho-cvc
/docs/quickstart.md                     @cho-cvc

# Wire spec — the normative document and its schemas are owned by the
# spec owner. Any change here requires an RFC per GOVERNANCE.md §5.
/docs/wire-spec-v1.0.md                 @cho-cvc
/docs/schemas/                          @cho-cvc
/docs/versioning-policy.md              @cho-cvc
/docs/vectors.md                        @cho-cvc

# Trust model — positioning-sensitive, requires spec-owner review.
/docs/trust-model.md                    @cho-cvc

# Reader documentation — owned by the reader-framework owner, with
# spec-owner co-review because reader docs describe schema mappings.
/docs/readers/                          @nickcontinentalvc @cho-cvc
/docs/readers/README.md                 @nickcontinentalvc @cho-cvc
/docs/readers/cloudtrail.md             @nickcontinentalvc @cho-cvc
/docs/readers/anthropic.md              @nickcontinentalvc @cho-cvc

# Golden vectors — wire-spec conformance artifacts. Changes require an
# RFC per GOVERNANCE.md §5.
/vectors/                               @cho-cvc

# Examples — Nick owns examples that exercise readers; Cho owns examples
# that exercise the core verification path.
/examples/                              @nickcontinentalvc @cho-cvc

